MID_EV11_019_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_019_m01_001: I can't believe someone bested the White-Maned\nDemon right here in Dagda!
MID_EV11_019_m01_002: Cruaidín's not normal. He's gotta be a famous\nfighter, right?
MID_EV11_019_m01_003: Yeah, you don't see that every day—the Demon\neating dirt.
MID_EV11_019_m01_004: I'm getting the impression we just saw something\nout of the ordinary.
MID_EV11_019_m01_005: So, uh... The other fighters in the games...they won't\nall be like that, will they?
MID_EV11_019_m01_006: We wouldn't stand a chance.
MID_EV11_019_m01_028: <NCA>Recall the fight.
MID_EV11_019_m01_007: The White-Maned Demon and Cruaidín...\nIncredible fighters, both of them.
MID_EV11_019_m01_008: The Demon's skills were so sharp. It's like he was\nslicing up the air in the arena. He was actually scary.
MID_EV11_019_m01_009: But Cruaidín seemed to anticipate every move.
MID_EV11_019_m01_011: And the crowd's reaction...
MID_EV11_019_m01_012: When the Demon lost, they couldn't believe it.
MID_EV11_019_m01_013: And Cruaidín? He's a cipher, totally unknown.
MID_EV11_019_m01_014: I tried asking around a little, but I couldn't find a\nsingle person who knew anything about him.
MID_EV11_019_m01_015: No way. Like a phantom or something?
MID_EV11_019_m01_016: Maybe he's a famous person fighting in disguise.
MID_EV11_019_m01_017: Could be. It's hard to even guess, with absolutely\nno information.
MID_EV11_019_m01_018: Well, what about the White-Maned Demon?
MID_EV11_019_m01_019: He seems well-known in Dagsion. Rumor has it he\nwas a general in Arago.
MID_EV11_019_m01_020: He was convicted of a dreadful crime and sentenced\nto some "Trial of the Chariot." It's ongoing, I guess.
MID_EV11_019_m01_021: Apparently, they keep him locked up in a dungeon\nunder the arena.
MID_EV11_019_m01_022: I've heard that's where Dagsion holds its criminals.
MID_EV11_019_m01_023: That means...Pop could be there too!
MID_EV11_019_m01_024: Oh... *gasp*
MID_EV11_019_m01_025: Since we're tournament participants, we're more or\nless event staff, right?
MID_EV11_019_m01_026: Maybe that status will get us into the hold beneath\nthe arena.
MID_EV11_019_m01_027: If we can pull it off, I might get to see Pop.
MID_EV11_020_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_020_m01_001: Um, excuse me...
MID_EV11_020_m01_002: What do you want?
MID_EV11_020_m01_003: Isn't there a jail up ahead...for Dagsion's criminals?
MID_EV11_020_m01_004: Could we possibly get in, look around?
MID_EV11_020_m01_005: Are you kidding me? That's idiotic! You think I just\nlet everyone in who asks politely?
MID_EV11_020_m01_008: This is no place for kids. Get outta here.
MID_EV11_020_m01_036: <NCA>Stand your ground.
MID_EV11_020_m01_009: Listen, I think my father's in there. If I could just say\na few words to him...
MID_EV11_020_m01_010: You need special permission from the temples, or you\ndon't get in. That's how it works.
MID_EV11_020_m01_011: I can't just let everyone in who wants in. I'll lose\nmy job.
MID_EV11_020_m01_013: Lady of Lilies... Is your business complete?
MID_EV11_020_m01_014: Yes. He doesn't seem to be suffering any aftereffects.\nBy appearances at least, he'll—
MID_EV11_020_m01_015: I'm sure he'll be thrilling us with a wonderful match\nin no time. Won't he, Babbu?
MID_EV11_020_m01_012: Oh! What are you little rascals doing in a place \nlike this?
MID_EV11_020_m01_037: <NCA>Explain the situation.
MID_EV11_020_m01_016: My father's in here. I just want to talk to him.
MID_EV11_020_m01_017: Interesting... Hmm... You're really quite cute, now\nthat I've gotten a look at you.
MID_EV11_020_m01_018: The brave boy comes to visit daddy in jail...\nSuch a lovely story, isn't it, Babbu?
MID_EV11_020_m01_019: Heeheehee. Ah... Gabriel, it's fine. Let these\nchildren pass.
MID_EV11_020_m01_020: Wh-what? I can't allow that! Rules are rules,\nafter all...
MID_EV11_020_m01_021: Perhaps you didn't hear me. I said this will be\nperfectly fine.
MID_EV11_020_m01_023: Really? Thank you! But, uh, who are you?
MID_EV11_020_m01_024: Ehehe. I am Iliana Ximinus, known by all as\nthe Lady of Lilies.
MID_EV11_020_m01_025: I'm here for the White-Maned Demon, as his\npatron, you might say.
MID_EV11_020_m01_026: I'm Cai of Ribeira village. Thanks again for helping\nme, Iliana.
MID_EV11_020_m01_027: Really, it's nothing. Take your time speaking with\nyour father.
MID_EV11_020_m01_028: The Lady of Lilies has taken a shine to you.\nYou're one lucky kid.
MID_EV11_020_m01_029: Huh...
MID_EV11_020_m01_030: Wow. She's beautiful, isn't she?
MID_EV11_020_m01_031: You two get a good-enough look?
MID_EV11_020_m01_032: Tialla, it's not like that.
MID_EV11_020_m01_033: It's just...something about her reminded me a little\nof my mom.
MID_EV11_020_m01_034: A child possessing Father's eye... Isn't that exactly\nwhat Big Sister said?
MID_EV11_020_m01_035: Ehehehehe. What a wonder if our destinies\nare entwined.
MID_EV11_021_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_021_m01_001: Pop! Thank goodness you're still alive!
MID_EV11_021_m01_002: Cai? What are you doing here?
MID_EV11_021_m01_003: I asked if I could get in to see you.
MID_EV11_021_m01_004: I had some trouble, but this kind lady came by, and\nshe told the guard to let us pass.
MID_EV11_021_m01_005: The lady who was just here? The Lady of Lilies...\nhelped you?
MID_EV11_021_m01_007: I told her why I was here, and I guess it made an\nimpression. Anyway, she let me through.
MID_EV11_021_m01_008: Hmm... I see. I've always thought she was\nkind of...different.
MID_EV11_021_m01_009: Never mind that. Listen, I've been doing some\nthinking about how to get you outta here.
MID_EV11_021_m01_010: So we entered the Heroic Games. We'll win, and\nwe'll ask for your freedom.
MID_EV11_021_m01_011: What?! Cai, that's insane.
MID_EV11_021_m01_013: It really is. I keep saying so.
MID_EV11_021_m01_014: Fantasies don't come true. You'll get hurt. This will\nend in tears.
MID_EV11_021_m01_015: I don't get it. This is the lesson the great "Windstorm\nCastor" gives to his child?
MID_EV11_021_m01_016: I guess it's true that I've trained Cai his whole life,\ntaught him fighting skills, if not wisdom.
MID_EV11_021_m01_032: <NCA>Share your feelings.
MID_EV11_021_m01_017: If I'm being honest, I'm not sure how far we can go.
MID_EV11_021_m01_018: But I can't sit by and do nothing. I can't just wait for\nthe end without trying to fix this.
MID_EV11_021_m01_019: And I've got Tialla and Peter helping me.
MID_EV11_021_m01_020: Damn it, kid. You really do have some loyal friends,\ndon't you?
MID_EV11_021_m01_021: I have to win this, Pop. I have to do everything I can\nto get you out of here.
MID_EV11_021_m01_022: You'll be free, and you and me and Mom can\nbe together.
MID_EV11_021_m01_024: Heh, you've got a knack for rash decisions. I wonder\nif you get that from me or your mother.
MID_EV11_021_m01_025: Well, you're the one who raised me, so I think it's\npretty obvious. No complaints though!
MID_EV11_021_m01_026: And since I'm allowed in here, I'll make the most of\nit and come see you as often as I can.
MID_EV11_021_m01_027: That's fine, but don't go making a spectacle of\nyourself down here.
MID_EV11_021_m01_028: Jail isn't a playground. Got it?
MID_EV11_021_m01_029: By the way, Mr. Castor, is there any chance you\nknow the White-Maned Demon?
MID_EV11_021_m01_030: Yeah, he's pretty famous, it seems. He's in a cell a\nlittle further from this one.
MID_EV11_021_m01_031: You kids should go meet him at least once. He's an\nimpressive fighter.
MID_EV11_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_022_m01_002: Who goes there?
MID_EV11_022_m01_003: Oh! Sorry. I wasn't trying to sneak up on you.
MID_EV11_022_m01_004: Peter! Please don't do that.
MID_EV11_022_m01_041: Oh! Sorry. I wasn't trying to sneak up on you.
MID_EV11_022_m01_042: Peter! Please don't do that.
MID_EV11_022_m01_005: Um... Mr. Demon, my name is Cai. We saw your\nmatch today.
MID_EV11_022_m01_006: You were so amazing to watch. So, I hoped that\nI could talk with you a little bit.
MID_EV11_022_m01_007: That kind of request doesn't normally get you into\nthis place.
MID_EV11_022_m01_008: Oh, my dad is here. He used to be a vulkan, but\nnow he's waiting to be executed.
MID_EV11_022_m01_009: That sounds...complicated.
MID_EV11_022_m01_010: I came here to see my dad, and someone called the\nLady of Lilies let me in.
MID_EV11_022_m01_011: Pop told me you were down here too, so I thought\nI'd try to talk to you.
MID_EV11_022_m01_012: Ahh. But I lost the exhibition match in pretty\nspectacular fashion.
MID_EV11_022_m01_013: Well, I for one am glad to see that your demon face is\njust for show.
MID_EV11_022_m01_014: What do you mean by that?
MID_EV11_022_m01_015: Honestly, we all thought you'd be terrifying.
MID_EV11_022_m01_017: But meeting you in person, you don't seem so scary.\nI'm...I'm relieved.
MID_EV11_022_m01_018: We've exchanged a few words. What do you think\nyou can learn from that?
MID_EV11_022_m01_019: It's in the eyes. I can see you're more than a fighter.
MID_EV11_022_m01_020: Uhm, Mr. Demon, how did you end up—
MID_EV11_022_m01_021: Bertrand. My name's Bertrand.
MID_EV11_022_m01_022: My friend betrayed me, so I'm stuck here fighting for\nmy freedom.
MID_EV11_022_m01_028: Bertrand... I have a favor to ask.
MID_EV11_022_m01_029: Will you teach me your fighting techniques?
MID_EV11_022_m01_030: Why would you need them?
MID_EV11_022_m01_031: I'm fighting in the Heroic Games to save\nmy father.
MID_EV11_022_m01_032: I need every advantage I can get, so I want to learn\nto fight like you.
MID_EV11_022_m01_033: A child. Fighting in the games.
MID_EV11_022_m01_034: Yeah, I'm a kid...an unstoppable kid.
MID_EV11_022_m01_035: I get it. We both have dreams we can't let go of.
MID_EV11_022_m01_036: The technique is inherited from my ancestor, but my\nstyle's my own.
MID_EV11_022_m01_037: If you really want to learn, I'll teach you.
MID_EV11_022_m01_038: Yes! Of course! Thank you so much, Mr. D—\nUh, Bertrand.
MID_EV11_070_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_070_m01_001: Hey! You three!
MID_EV11_070_m01_002: I've been looking for you for ages! Ribeira Winds,\nam I right?
MID_EV11_070_m01_003: Exactly! But who are you?
MID_EV11_070_m01_004: Heeheehee. I'm Anna, Dagsion's most mysterious\nmatchmaker.
MID_EV11_070_m01_005: By which I mean I work for the temples in organizing\nmatches for the Heroic Games.
MID_EV11_070_m01_006: I might not look it, but I hold the rank of attendant\npriest in the temple of Solel.
MID_EV11_070_m01_007: Attendant priest? Is that something to brag about?\nIt's pretty far down the ladder if I remember right.
MID_EV11_070_m01_008: It goes: archpriest, high priest, lead priest, ritual\npriest, attendant priest, assistant, apprentice.
MID_EV11_070_m01_009: So yeah, she's not that high up.
MID_EV11_070_m01_010: Rude! I can hear you!
MID_EV11_070_m01_025: <NCA>Ask what she needs.
MID_EV11_070_m01_011: So, uh, what can we do for you, Anna?
MID_EV11_070_m01_012: Listen. We've set the dates and opponents for\nyour qualifier.
MID_EV11_070_m01_013: Get familiar with the details. They're in this letter.
MID_EV11_070_m01_014: <TLP>Ribeira Winds\n\nMatch: First Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Gaia Brigade\nLeader: Zarcone\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV11_070_m01_015: You might know this already—more than three\nthousand clans are fighting in the games. 
MID_EV11_070_m01_016: We need to thin out the ranks a bit, so the qualifying\nrounds are sort of a cooperative competition.
MID_EV11_070_m01_017: What I mean is it won't be just your clan against\nanother. You'll have other clans on your side.
MID_EV11_070_m01_018: If you want to win, you'll need to cooperate\neffectively with the other clans on your team.
MID_EV11_070_m01_019: On that note, make sure you get yourselves properly\nprepared. Time is running out.
MID_EV11_070_m01_020: Questions?
MID_EV11_070_m01_021: Can you tell us which clans are on our team?
MID_EV11_070_m01_022: The rules say I can't. Besides, the pairings might\nchange depending on how the other qualifiers go.
MID_EV11_070_m01_023: You'll probably have to wait until the day of.
MID_EV11_070_m01_024: Thanks, Anna.
MID_EV11_104_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_104_m01_001: Bertrand! Ready for training?
MID_EV11_104_m01_002: Back again? Enthusiastic as ever, I see.
MID_EV11_104_m01_003: I need to get much, much better.
MID_EV11_104_m01_004: And you know what? You're a great teacher. Your\nstyle is different than Pop's. It's actually fun.
MID_EV11_104_m01_005: I'm glad you're getting something out of it. You have\nthe aptitude, so it feels like this is worth my time.
MID_EV11_104_m01_006: Today we train with swords. I'm going to teach you\nsome techniques handed down through my family.
MID_EV11_104_m01_007: Great! I'm ready to go anytime.
MID_EV11_104_m01_008: Let's leave it there for today.
MID_EV11_104_m01_009: Too much training will have diminishing returns.\nGet yourself some food and rest.
MID_EV11_104_m01_010: Thanks, Bertrand. How'm I doing? Getting better?
MID_EV11_104_m01_011: That's for you to decide.
MID_EV11_104_m01_012: Good training is like a friend that will never betray\nyou. Pay in sweat, get it back in strength.
MID_EV11_104_m01_013: Repetition is key. Do what I've taught you, every day.
MID_EV11_104_m01_014: You said you trained under someone before, right?
MID_EV11_104_m01_015: Pop's been hammering this fighting stuff into me\nsince I was little.
MID_EV11_104_m01_016: You've got a solid grasp of the basics, but I can tell\nyou've picked up some advanced techniques too.
MID_EV11_104_m01_017: Your mentor must be something of an expert. I have\nto say, I'm curious.
MID_EV11_104_m01_018: You're fighting for your father, right? To save him?
MID_EV11_104_m01_019: Right. He used to be a temple vulkan. That's what\nhe told me.
MID_EV11_104_m01_020: But then, he found himself in one of these cells.
MID_EV11_104_m01_021: Ahh, that's right. Your skill level makes more sense if\na vulkan trained you.
MID_EV11_104_m01_022: Pop wanted me strong enough and good enough to\nhandle life's challenges by myself, I think.
MID_EV11_104_m01_023: Now he's just accepted his fate. So he's sitting in a\ncell waiting to die.
MID_EV11_104_m01_024: I hate that he's taking it like that, like he's given up.\nIf I win, I can save him, and it'll make Mom happy.
MID_EV11_104_m01_025: I think your father's proud of you, Cai, as any father\nwould be.
MID_EV11_104_m01_026: Keep your eyes on the prize. I'll be cheering for you\nfrom the shadows.
MID_EV11_104_m01_027: Yes, sir! Thanks, Bertrand!
MID_EV11_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_024_m01_001: This is only a qualifier, but there's so much to see,\nso many fighters.
MID_EV11_024_m01_002: This is making me nervous. Are we really gonna\nmake it through in one piece?
MID_EV11_024_m01_030: This is making me nervous. Are we really gonna\nmake it through in one piece?
MID_EV11_024_m01_003: I heard we'll be split into east and west sides, with\nmultiple clans cooperating on each side.
MID_EV11_024_m01_004: But we can boil down the actual fight to one simple\nrule: Defeat every enemy we run into.
MID_EV11_024_m01_005: It's the boy. Why is he in my presence again?
MID_EV11_024_m01_006: It-it's her!
MID_EV11_024_m01_052: It-it's her!
MID_EV11_024_m01_007: Oh! The lady from Saramis, from the other day.
MID_EV11_024_m01_008: Hey! How dare you show up here after what you did\nto Cai!
MID_EV11_024_m01_009: I feel a headache coming on. Do these children's\nparents know they're here?
MID_EV11_024_m01_010: Sorry, boss. We're fresh out of headache treatment.
MID_EV11_024_m01_012: Thank goodness I made it in time! I'm looking\nforward to working with you all today.
MID_EV11_024_m01_013: The cat priest? You're in the tournament too?
MID_EV11_024_m01_014: Nice to see you, Theodora. Yes, we're taking part too.
MID_EV11_024_m01_015: Something seems amiss here.
MID_EV11_024_m01_016: It is quite the gathering of souls bound by threads\nof causality.
MID_EV11_024_m01_017: They say meeting by chance...is getting tangled in a\nthread from a previous life. Maybe fate connects us.
MID_EV11_024_m01_018: Gotta say, you're one lucky kid. Hope you're not still\nsmarting from last time.
MID_EV11_024_m01_019: I'm fine. What do you mean, "lucky kid"?
MID_EV11_024_m01_020: If the boss hadn't stepped in at the procession,\nit woulda been curtains for you.
MID_EV11_024_m01_021: The law of Saramis says anyone who interrupts a\nroyal procession gets put to death.
MID_EV11_024_m01_022: We're a seafaring people, and rules are big on a ship.\nSo we take this stuff serious.
MID_EV11_024_m01_023: S-sure. And you're all still mad at me for breaking\nthose rules?
MID_EV11_024_m01_024: Nah. The boss has taken kind of a shine to you,\nactually. See what I mean about being lucky?
MID_EV11_024_m01_025: Really?
MID_EV11_024_m01_026: Enough idle chatter, Tobias. The gates are opening.
MID_EV11_024_m01_027: O goddess who watches over us from on high...
MID_EV11_024_m01_028: Bring us victory this day. We offer our souls and\ndedicate this fight to Yu Phas!
MID_EV11_024_m01_029: We offer our souls and dedicate this fight to Yu Phas!
MID_EV11_024_m01_031: Yu Phas... Isn't she my mom's mom?
MID_EV11_024_m01_032: The people of Saramis have great reverence for her.
MID_EV11_024_m01_033: She's the goddess of death though, right? Is it really\nOK to revere death?
MID_EV11_024_m01_053: She's the goddess of death though, right? Is it really\nOK to revere death?
MID_EV11_024_m01_034: Whatever the case, I think things are gonna go a\nlittle better with our new partners.
MID_EV11_024_m01_035: Cai, I don't think it's as simple as that.
MID_EV11_024_m01_054: Cai, I don't think it's as simple as that.
MID_EV11_024_m01_036: Diego, that prayer... What was that all about?
MID_EV11_024_m01_037: It's a battle prayer passed down by the forest people,\ndescendants of the Damascar people.
MID_EV11_024_m01_038: Hmm... Well, take good care of your own soul, please.
MID_EV11_024_m01_039: You mustn't waste something so precious.
MID_EV11_024_m01_041: Baw haw haw! That's a funny way of telling us to\ntry not to die.
MID_EV11_024_m01_042: So long as you do not hinder us, there will be no\nproblems. Got it?
MID_EV11_024_m01_043: Got it. I'll do my very best. Only...
MID_EV11_024_m01_044: I intend to win for my own reasons.
MID_EV11_024_m01_045: Hey, I heard what you said a second ago. You\nwouldn't be from the forest yourself, huh?
MID_EV11_024_m01_046: That's got nothing to do with me, not anymore.
MID_EV11_024_m01_047: What I said about not hindering us goes for you\nas well, children.
MID_EV11_024_m01_048: If you must play at being warriors, stay well back.\nLet us engage the enemy.
MID_EV11_024_m01_049: Sounds good! Thanks...Sis.
MID_EV11_024_m01_050: "Sis"?
MID_EV11_024_m01_051: Even my brother doesn't call me that.
MID_EV11_071_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_071_m01_001: Hear me, patrons of the games! I have a question for\nyou all. Are you familiar with the Mons Uprising?
MID_EV11_071_m01_002: It seems you are. This family feud in the kingdom of\nBrezarant threatened to cleave the nation in twain!
MID_EV11_071_m01_003: The year is 1232 by the Dagdan Calendar, and the\nturmoil of the infamous Zodiac Incident lingers still.
MID_EV11_071_m01_004: In the fortress city of Mons, fourth prince Helmeric\nraised an army, supported by the Chetaur people.
MID_EV11_071_m01_005: They began their march to the royal capital Breston,\nwhere King Marius readied himself.
MID_EV11_071_m01_006: And it is here, at the Pallas Bridge, where the two\narmies shall stand against each other.
MID_EV11_071_m01_007: In the Eastern Division, the brave Gaia Brigade, led\nby the fighter Zarcone, represents Helmeric's forces.
MID_EV11_071_m01_008: In the Western Division, warriors led by Queen\nTheodora of Saramis play the army of King Marius!
MID_EV11_071_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV11_071_m01_010: Bonaventure. What do you know of our foes?
MID_EV11_071_m01_011: They are a mixed squadron. At their core is Gaia\nBrigade, a gang of thieves.
MID_EV11_071_m01_012: They have a handful of skilled fighters but none\nthat should trouble us overmuch.
MID_EV11_071_m01_013: Their leader, Zarcone, has lately been a highwayman\nin the mountains north of Caelus.
MID_EV11_071_m01_014: In sum, he is a minor annoyance with no prospects\nbeyond preying on the weak.
MID_EV11_071_m01_015: Clear and thorough. Typically excellent work from\nSaramis's chief intelligence officer.
MID_EV11_071_m01_016: Your praise is my delight, Your Majesty.
MID_EV11_071_m01_017: Damn, Bona. You hear something once, and you\nremember it forever.
MID_EV11_071_m01_018: As for our allies...
MID_EV11_071_m01_019: For starters, we're teamed with a clan led by an odd,\nI suppose...priest? She wears a bizarre cat mask.
MID_EV11_071_m01_020: Then we have what looks at first blush to be a\nragtag assemblage of street urchins.
MID_EV11_071_m01_021: Not of noble stock, that much is certain.
MID_EV11_071_m01_022: Other than that, I have no intelligence on them.\nThey are utterly unknown quantities.
MID_EV11_071_m01_023: I feel a hand at work in this matchup. I suspect the\ntemples have their own agenda... I am not amused.
MID_EV11_071_m01_024: Still, the boy and the cat priest intrigue me.
MID_EV11_071_m01_025: Somewhat cynical of you, Your Majesty, but I find\nyour reasoning sound.
MID_EV11_071_m01_026: The child was callow enough to halt my procession.\nHe is either full of courage or lacking in brains.
MID_EV11_071_m01_027: Or...perhaps he is driven by a burden all his own.
MID_EV11_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_025_m01_001: Yeah! That's one win in the qualifiers!
MID_EV11_025_m01_002: Somehow, we won. Not bad.
MID_EV11_025_m01_003: Peter, you did great! You've got some skills!
MID_EV11_025_m01_004: How'd I do, Diego? Did I hold my own out there?
MID_EV11_025_m01_005: You were remarkable, Orchel.
MID_EV11_025_m01_006: A truly splendid showing, Your Majesty.
MID_EV11_025_m01_007: No need to praise me for crushing insects underfoot.
MID_EV11_025_m01_008: May I ask you something? Your arm... Do you mind if\nI take a look?
MID_EV11_025_m01_009: I...suppose not. It is only an arm.
MID_EV11_025_m01_011: Your arm... I sense an ominous strength in it. If you\ncontinue to use something like this—
MID_EV11_025_m01_012: It is the arm of the hero Mahadu, a legend among\nthe forest peoples.
MID_EV11_025_m01_014: It paved the way for my ascension to the throne.\nI was aware of its "ominous" aspects already.
MID_EV11_025_m01_015: I appreciate the spirit in which your advice was\ngiven, but it is none of your concern.
MID_EV11_025_m01_016: Nothing good comes of such objects. You need to\nguard yourself—and your soul—better.
MID_EV11_025_m01_018: As you say. Let us both mind our own souls.
MID_EV11_025_m01_019: Cai? It's Cai, isn't it? May I see your left hand, please?
MID_EV11_025_m01_020: Huh? Me? Sure, but this jewel doesn't come off, just\nso you know.
MID_EV11_025_m01_021: Hmm... Another one...
MID_EV11_025_m01_027: Cai, where did you get this jewel?
MID_EV11_025_m01_028: I was told it belonged to my mother.
MID_EV11_025_m01_030: By any chance, is your mother connected to a\ntemple somehow?
MID_EV11_025_m01_031: Sort of. But I can't get into the details.
MID_EV11_025_m01_032: You know, you kind of remind me of my\nmom, Orchel.
MID_EV11_025_m01_033: Oh? Is that so?
MID_EV11_025_m01_036: So many questions, and yet you have said nothing\nof your own uncanny body.
MID_EV11_025_m01_037: Oh! Sorry, I-I have to be on my way. Diego?
MID_EV11_025_m01_038: What? Oh! Right, yes.
MID_EV11_025_m01_039: Let's be off then, Diego. Take care, all!
MID_EV11_025_m01_040: Orchel! Slow down! Not so fast!
MID_EV11_025_m01_041: What in the world?
MID_EV11_025_m01_042: It matters not. Let a woman keep her secrets.
MID_EV11_025_m01_043: She's not...normal, is she?
MID_EV11_025_m01_044: She outwardly appears so at least.
MID_EV11_025_m01_045: You are beginning to pique my interest, Cai.
MID_EV11_025_m01_046: I get it. I'm wondering if my jewel and your arm...\nAre they...
MID_EV11_025_m01_047: I thought the same. They may carry a similar power,\nthough one that manifests in different ways.
MID_EV11_025_m01_048: If so, then I would caution you not to rely overmuch\non the jewel's abilities.
MID_EV11_025_m01_049: Right. It gives me a strange feeling, so I'm trying not\nto overdo it.
MID_EV11_025_m01_050: Anyway, I'd better get going too. Catch you later,\nTheodora! Everyone!
MID_EV11_025_m01_051: The Heroic Games may put us at odds with the boy\nat some point.
MID_EV11_025_m01_052: He is a callow youth now. But in a few years' time,\nI can see him coming into his own.
MID_EV11_025_m01_053: Baw haw haw! You saying he could be husband\nmaterial, boss? Bona and I would flip!
MID_EV11_025_m01_054: Silence! I have made my stance on this subject clear.
MID_EV11_025_m01_055: I will entertain no suitor incapable of surpassing my\nown strength.
MID_EV11_025_m01_056: Yeah, but, boss, that rules out everyone in Saramis...
MID_EV11_026_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_026_m01_001: Ah, wonderful! That was truly an exhilarating fight.
MID_EV11_026_m01_002: The power they demonstrate out there... It can't be\nthe power of mere mortals, can it?
MID_EV11_026_m01_003: It... It calls to mind the prowess of Hanno and his\nBloodaxe that I saw so long ago.
MID_EV11_026_m01_004: Perhaps I ought to ask them about it.
MID_EV11_026_m01_005: What does it matter? If they have the strength, they\nwin the fight, simple as that.
MID_EV11_026_m01_006: What's important is such contenders will add a\ndelightful splash of color to future bouts.
MID_EV11_026_m01_007: It might be better to put our questions to them after\nthe festivities...don't you think?
MID_EV11_026_m01_008: Yes, you're probably correct about that.
MID_EV11_026_m01_009: Ah... In any case, it was an excellent fight, yes?
MID_EV11_026_m01_010: Theodora, queen of Saramis, rose above the others in\npure strength—a truly wonderful warrior.
MID_EV11_026_m01_011: The might of the Shield of Dagda is even greater\nthan the rumors have it.
MID_EV11_026_m01_012: Certainly. And in addition to the Saraminians, some\nintriguing people have gathered for the event.
MID_EV11_026_m01_013: Come what may, it will be an entertaining\ntournament.
MID_EV11_026_m01_014: Solel, do you think me...
MID_EV11_026_m01_015: Do you think me an atrocious woman, thirsting for\nblood as I do?
MID_EV11_026_m01_016: Absurd. You don't really believe that's how I see you,\ndo you?
MID_EV11_026_m01_017: I...I'm no good at all. Everything I might have once\nleaned upon for support, it's all lost to me.
MID_EV11_026_m01_018: Not a shred of my memory has returned, and my\ntrue self is beyond my grasp. It's as if I'm in a haze.
MID_EV11_026_m01_019: It's only when I see another's blood flow that I can\ntruly feel the raw essence of my own life.
MID_EV11_026_m01_020: Only then can I feel something returning, some\nrecollection of myself. 
MID_EV11_026_m01_021: But just as that feeling comes on, I become\nunbearably afraid of who I am.
MID_EV11_026_m01_024: It doesn't have to be right away, but whenever you\nfeel ready, let's visit our daughter, Aurora.
MID_EV11_026_m01_025: I'm sure she'll be overjoyed to see you.
MID_EV11_026_m01_026: There's no rush to recover your memories. We have\nall the time in the world.
MID_EV11_026_m01_027: Don't we, my precious Yu Phas?